  "answer_text": "To book your round-trip (return) train ticket from Boston to New York, you will need to book through **Amtrak**, the sole operator for this route. \n\nBased on today's date, \"next Friday\" is **Friday, June 5, 2026**. Because you requested a *return* ticket, you will need to choose a return date (for example, Sunday, June 7, 2026, if you are planning a weekend trip).\n\nAs an AI, I cannot process payments or make direct purchases on your behalf, but I can guide you to book this instantly at the best price.\n\n### Step 1: Choose Your Train Option\nAmtrak offers two main services between Boston and New York:\n*   **Northeast Regional:** The most common and budget-friendly option. It takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**.\n*   **Acela:** Amtrak\u2019s high-speed train. It takes about **3 hours and 40 minutes**, features more premium amenities, but is more expensive.\n\n### Step 2: Book Your Tickets Online\nYou can book your tickets directly using one of the following official platforms:\n\n1.  **Amtrak Official Website:** Go to [Amtrak Tickets & Reservations](https://www.amtrak.com/tickets-reservations.html) to search and purchase.\n2.  **Google Flights (Now lists Amtrak):** You can compare train times and easily click through to book by searching on [Google Flights](https://www.google.com/flights). \n\n### Step 3: Enter Your Travel Details\nWhen booking, use the following details to ensure you get the correct stations:\n*   **From:** Boston, MA \u2013 South Station (BOS) *or* Back Bay Station (BBY)\n*   **To:** New York, NY \u2013 Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP)\n*   **Departure Date:** Friday, June 5, 2026\n*   **Return Date:** [Select your preferred return date, e.g., Sunday, June 7, 2026]\n*   **Passengers:** [Number of travelers]\n\n### Travel Tips\n*   **Book ASAP:** Friday is a peak travel day on the Northeast Corridor. Fares will rise significantly as the departure date approaches, so booking today will lock in the lowest possible 